  /// corresponds to the version of the source code you want to build. If a
  /// pull request ID is specified, it must use the format pr/pull-request-ID
  /// (for example pr/25 ). If a branch name is specified, the branch's HEAD
  /// commit ID is used. If not specified, the default branch's HEAD commit ID
  /// is used. For GitLab: the commit ID, branch, or Git tag to use. For
  /// Bitbucket: the commit ID, branch name, or tag name that corresponds to
  /// the version of the source code you want to build. If a branch name is
  /// specified, the branch's HEAD commit ID is used. If not specified, the
  /// default branch's HEAD commit ID is used. For Amazon S3: the version ID
  /// of the object that represents the build input ZIP file to use. If
  /// sourceVersion is specified at the build level, then that version takes
  /// precedence over this sourceVersion (at the project level). For more
  /// information, see Source Version Sample with CodeBuild in the CodeBuild
  /// User Guide .
  pub source_version: Str? = None
  /// An array of ProjectSourceVersion objects. If secondarySourceVersions is
  /// specified at the build level, then they take over these
  /// secondarySourceVersions (at the project level).
  pub secondary_source_versions: List[ProjectSourceVersion]? = None
  /// Information about the build output artifacts for the build project.
  pub artifacts: ProjectArtifacts? = None
  /// An array of ProjectArtifacts objects.
  pub secondary_artifacts: List[ProjectArtifacts]? = None
  /// Information about the cache for the build project.
  pub cache: ProjectCache? = None
  /// Information about the build environment for this build project.
  pub environment: ProjectEnvironment? = None
  /// The ARN of the IAM role that enables CodeBuild to interact with
  /// dependent Amazon Web Services services on behalf of the Amazon Web
  /// Services account.
  pub service_role: Str? = None
  /// How long, in minutes, from 5 to 2160 (36 hours), for CodeBuild to wait
  /// before timing out any related build that did not get marked as
  /// completed. The default is 60 minutes.
  pub timeout_in_minutes: Int? = None
  /// The number of minutes a build is allowed to be queued before it times
  /// out.
  pub queued_timeout_in_minutes: Int? = None
  /// The Key Management Service customer master key (CMK) to be used for
  /// encrypting the build output artifacts. You can use a cross-account KMS
  /// key to encrypt the build output artifacts if your service role has
  /// permission to that key. You can specify either the Amazon Resource Name
  /// (ARN) of the CMK or, if available, the CMK's alias (using the format
  /// alias/ ). If you don't specify a value, CodeBuild uses the managed CMK
  /// for Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3).
